{
  "format": "ma3sc-plan",
  "version": 1,
  "notes": "Techno contrast revision. Rig seen from FOH: 4 MH 100 Beam heads in a 2x2 block (left 101 back / 103 front, right 102 back / 104 front), 4 Root Par 6 nearest the audience, 4 Stagepar QCL upstage, 2 Sunstrips low at the very back. Contrast first: no BASE look lights the whole rig evenly any more; most leave whole fixture types dark (front pars off in four of five bases, 'Beams only' lights the heads alone), so the picture is made of lit and dark areas. Effects are on/off shapes only (chase, snap_on/snap_off with full-cycle spreads, left/right ping-pong at 0 and 180 degrees); the soft dim_sinus waves and the rainbow are gone. Colours are saturated pairs with no pastel and no mixed white except where white is the point: red/white, cyan/magenta left-right, acid green/magenta, blue/amber depth, fire and ice, cold white/blue, and deep red mono for calm parts. Colour FX layer: hard two-colour phasers, each on one fixture type only (heads white/red, front pars cyan/magenta, stage pars red/blue). Real strobe: the STROBE looks run the strobe phasers at Mul4 (four flashes per beat, about 8.5 Hz at 128 BPM). A riser look ramps a strobe in over the build. Separation rule (user request): no sequence mixes static values with phasers, and no sequence mixes phaser kinds (dimmer chasers never share a sequence with colour phasers), so a sequence that is fired again or left running can never leave a stray static state behind a chaser. Every sequence is therefore either all-static (BASE, COLOR, ACCENT, BLINDER, BLACKOUT), all dimmer phasers (EFFECT, Pars, RISER, STROBE) or all colour phasers (Colour FX). Consequence: the strobes no longer force white; they flash in the colour of the running COLOR look. One deliberate exception: MOVEMENT cues keep a static pan/tilt offset next to the position phaser on the same heads, because the position phasers are relative and without the offset the heads would swing around straight down; both lines touch only pan/tilt, never dimmer or colour, and the plan format has no other way to give a relative phaser its centre. Layers as before: default MOVEMENT moves the back heads 101/102, layer 'Front heads' moves 103/104; default EFFECT works on heads + sunstrips, layer 'Pars' on Root Pars + Stagepars, so no two layers touch the same attributes. BLACKOUT sequences run at High priority. Left out: Haze and Fog (no haze or fog fixture in this rig).",
